---
import RouteShell from "../../../components/RouteShell.astro";
export const prerender = true;
const url = "https://www.miamiknifeguy.com/learn/restaurant-knife-handoff/";
const schema = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Article", headline: "How Does After-Hours Restaurant Knife Handoff Work?", datePublished: "2026-10-03", dateModified: "2026-10-03", author: { "@id": "https://www.miamiknifeguy.com/#business" }, publisher: { "@id": "https://www.miamiknifeguy.com/#business" }, mainEntityOfPage: url };
---
<RouteShell title="After-Hours Restaurant Knife Handoff | Miami Knife Guy" description="Sharp After Dark plans pickup after a kitchen's last ticket and return before prep the next day for confirmed accounts within agreed service areas and schedules." canonicalPath="/learn/restaurant-knife-handoff/" schema={schema}>
  <main class="panel" aria-hidden="false"><article class="panel-inner max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <nav class="intake-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/learn/">← Knife care articles</a></nav>
    <p class="sub-eyebrow">Restaurant kitchens · Updated October 3, 2026</p>
    <h1 class="sub-headline-pink text-4xl lg:text-5xl mb-6">How does after-hours restaurant knife handoff work?</h1>
    <p class="sub-body mb-8">For a confirmed Sharp After Dark account in an agreed area and schedule, MKG picks up knives <strong class="text-white">after the last ticket</strong> and returns them <strong class="text-white">before prep the next day</strong>. The plan is built around the kitchen's actual hours, not a fixed clock window.</p>
    <div class="space-y-8 text-white/80 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      <section><h2 class="text-white text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">What if service ends late?</h2><p>Tell Sean when the last ticket is expected and who can hand off the knives. That may be 9 PM or midnight. MKG confirms the pickup time against your location, route, and the schedule agreed for the account.</p></section>
      <section><h2 class="text-white text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">What if prep starts early?</h2><p>Share the next day's prep start and return contact. Whether prep starts at 8 AM or noon, the agreed return is scheduled before prep. If the route or workload cannot support that schedule, Sean will discuss the available terms before confirming service.</p></section>
      <section><h2 class="text-white text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Which knives should be included?</h2><p>Count chef and prep knives, specialty blades, and dining-room steak knives. Mention chips, broken tips, serrations, and any knives that must stay on the line. A recurring program can include condition notes and fleet tracking.</p></section>
      <section><h2 class="text-white text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">How do I request the program?</h2><p>Send the restaurant name and location, approximate knife count, last-ticket time, next-prep time, preferred service days, and handoff contacts. One-time restaurant resets start at $150; recurring programs typically start at $250 per month, with final pricing based on the fleet, repairs, timing, and route.</p></section>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 mt-10"><a class="panel-cta-btn panel-cta-pink" href="/book/restaurant/?intent=sharp-after-dark">Request Sharp After Dark</a><a class="panel-cta-btn panel-cta-ghost" href="/sharp-after-dark/">View Program</a></div>
  </article></main>
</RouteShell>
